              "source": "Chapter lengkap",
              "content": [
                "The bridge of the Iron Behemoth no longer smelled of scorched oil, burning coal, and burnt blood; instead, it smelled strongly of jasmine, damp earth, and fresh rain. It was a staggering contrast to the suffocating stench that usually accompanied the Ash Empire's most fearsome dreadnought.",
                "Commander Vane, a massive man encased in thick, pressurized power-armor, strained against his bindings with every ounce of his enhanced mythic strength. It was entirely useless. He was not held captive by heavy iron chains or standard magical energy shields. Instead, ancient oak roots had erupted directly from the iron floorboards, holding his limbs in an unbreakable, yet surprisingly gentle, embrace. The more he struggled, the tighter the living wood seemed to hold him, adapting to his immense physical force with the effortless grace of nature.",
                "To add insult to his absolute defeat, a particularly pristine cluster of white lilies had bloomed directly over his main navigation helm, completely burying the ship's control console under a fragrant blanket of petals.",
                "\"Get these weeds off me!\" Vane roared, his voice muffled by a thick canopy of wisteria vines that draped elegantly from the ceiling. He thrashed violently, and while the thick armor plating of his suit creaked under the strain, the ancient wood refused to yield a single inch.",
                "A soft, cool sea breeze drifted through the shattered viewport of the dreadnought, clearing away the last remnants of toxic smog. Through that opening, Helena floated gracefully onto the blooming deck, her white overcoat completely unblemished by the chaos she had just orchestrated. Floating gently behind her, carried securely by a soft cushion of manipulated air, was the wounded scout, Kael.",
                "Helena had not uttered a single word or drawn a magical circle to bring him here; she simply wove her will into the fabric of the world.",
                "[Master Wind: Zephyr's Embrace]",
                "She gently lowered the injured scout onto a bed of soft, glowing moss that had completely overtaken the cold steel plates of the bridge. Kael’s breath hitched. He stared in absolute, paralyzing shock at the impossible sight outside the shattered window; the terrifying Armada of Ash, fifty invincible dreadnoughts of the Outer Expanse, had been transformed into a fleet of floating botanical gardens. The terrifying hum of enslaved leylines was gone, replaced by the gentle rustling of leaves.",
                "\"Commander Vane...\" Kael choked out, his bloodshot eyes darting frantically from the blooming flowers around him to his bound, helpless leader. His mind fractured trying to comprehend the sheer scale of the magic. \"The fleet... the Primal Mana engines...\".",
                "\"Your Primal Mana is currently fertilizing a very lovely patch of daisies on the lower decks,\" Helena interrupted smoothly, her tone conversational. She found an intact metal crate covered in ivy and gracefully sat upon it, pulling her delicate porcelain teapot from her dimensional pocket. \"I must say, raw, unfiltered energy makes for excellent compost\".",
                "As she arranged her tea set, Helena’s ancient mind drifted back to the First Era. She remembered Silas, her old companion, spending weeks trying to design magical machinery that wouldn't poison the earth. He had failed, lamenting that true progress always left a scar. If only you could see this, Silas, she thought with a quiet, nostalgic melancholy. I finally managed to build your green machines. It just required forcefully dismantling an empire's armada to do it.",
                "\"You witch!\" Vane snarled, interrupting her peaceful reminiscence as he thrashed violently against the oak roots once more. \"The Ash Emperor will burn this soft world to cinders! You cannot hold the Iron Fleet forever! When our reinforcements arrive—\".",
                "\"Commander,\" Helena said, her voice instantly dropping its polite cadence and taking on the heavy, resonant authority of the Ancient Sage.",
                "The ambient mana in the room suddenly solidified. It wasn't a direct attack, but rather the sheer, crushing weight of a predator at the absolute top of the food chain asserting its presence. The air grew so dense it felt like standing at the bottom of an ocean. Vane’s breath hitched in his throat, his arrogant sneer instantly dissolving into primal terror as his survival instincts finally recognized the incomprehensible abyss of power sitting before him.",
                "\"I have spent five thousand years ensuring that blood does not stain these beaches,\" Helena continued softly, her sapphire eyes glowing with a terrifying, cold light that illuminated the dim bridge. \"I did not destroy your ships because I am a pacifist. I transformed them because I abhor a mess. Do not mistake my mercy for weakness\".",
                "The oppressive weight vanished as quickly as it had appeared, leaving the two Ash Empire soldiers gasping for breath. She elegantly poured a cup of chamomile tea, allowing the sweet scent of honey to fill the tense air.",
                "\"It seems my quiet vacation at Cape Terminus is officially over,\" Helena sighed, her glowing eyes dimming back to their normal, serene sapphire as she looked toward the distant, peaceful cliffs of Eleanor. \"I suppose I must inform the capital that we have unexpected guests\".",
                "She set her teacup down delicately and raised her pale, bare hand. She closed her eyes, effortlessly tapping into the newly purified leylines that stretched across the continent.",
                "[Grandmaster Spatial: Leyline Whisper]",
                "She did not shout, nor did she rely on modern communication crystals. She simply projected her thoughts into the ambient flow of the world, directly targeting the specific mana signatures of the two greatest leaders of the modern era.",
                "\"My dear Archmage Valerius. Little Saintess,\" Helena's voice echoed directly into their minds, traversing thousands of miles to reach the Holy See in a fraction of a second. \"It appears the Mists of the End have fallen, and fifty iron warships from the Outer Expanse have docked at my beach. The crew is entirely unharmed, though quite tangled in my garden. I would appreciate it if you could summon the leaders of Aethelgard to the capital. We have some diplomatic matters to discuss regarding our new neighbors\".",
                "Helena lowered her hand and picked her teacup back up, taking a delicate sip to appreciate the perfect temperature. She looked over the rim of her cup at the utterly defeated Commander Vane and the trembling Kael.",
                "\"The leaders of this world will want to speak with you,\" Helena smiled, a polite, grandmotherly expression returning to her flawless face. \"I highly suggest you practice your manners before we arrive. The Archmage is quite particular about etiquette\"."
              ],
              "summary": "Kael dan Commander Vane dari Armada Besi terjebak di dalam kapal mereka sendiri yang kini ditumbuhi akar dan bunga raksasa. Sihir Helena tidak menyakiti, namun melumpuhkan mereka sepenuhnya. Helena mengirim pesan sopan ke ibu kota Aethelgard."
