              "title": "The Root Beneath Iron",
              "arcId": "arc-5",
              "arcTitle": "Echoes Beneath the Iron Sky",
              "status": "full",
              "source": "Chapter lengkap",
              "content": [
                "When the forge settled, the lower heart opened beneath the spiral. There, under heavenly metal and ancient frost, was a root.",
                "It was not large compared to the World Tree visions Helena had seen. No thicker than an old bridge, perhaps. But it pulsed with green-gold light that made every metal surface in the chamber reflect leaves. Yggdravael had touched Iron-Peak long ago. Not enough to awaken the continent. Enough to remember it.",
                "Valerius cried. He claimed later it was due to mana pressure, but no one believed him. Vane knelt to sketch the root and stopped, realizing some things became smaller when drawn too quickly. Elara placed a hand near it and smiled through exhaustion. Kael stood guard because roots, in his view, were not exempt from suspicion simply because they glowed beautifully.",
                "Helena approached last. The root did not call her the Ancient Sage. It did not call her Vessel. It did not call her Zenith. It touched her palm with a thread of light and showed her Skyforge Station above, Frost-Bight beyond, Aethelgard farther still, and countless roads sleeping inside the world.",
                "Then it showed her a distant continent where the true World Tree waited, vast and green beneath a sky full of leaves. Helena understood. Not yet. But someday. Iron-Peak's root was not a door to the stars. It was a promise that the doors existed."
              ],
              "summary": "When the forge settled, the lower heart opened beneath the spiral. There, under heavenly metal and ancient frost, was a root. It was not large compared to the World Tree visions Helena had seen. No thicker than an old bridge, perhaps. But...",
