              "title": "Frost Inside the Hourglass",
              "arcId": "arc-6",
              "arcTitle": "The City Where Time Sleeps",
              "status": "full",
              "source": "Chapter lengkap",
              "content": [
                "The village elder did not remember meeting them. He remembered meeting them. Both statements were true, depending on where he stood in the room. Near the hearth he greeted Helena as a stranger. Near the window he thanked her for coming back. At the table he wept because his wife had died yesterday, though Elara could see the woman outside hanging laundry beneath the repeated dawn.",
                "In the elder's cupboard, Valerius found an hourglass filled not with sand, but with powdered frost-mana. Every grain fell from the lower bulb into the upper one. When turned upside down, it politely ignored gravity and continued doing so. The glass was carved with the crest of Eirvalen: a tower, a sleeping eye, and a crescent moon caught between two clock hands.",
                "Elara held the hourglass and flinched. 'There are prayers inside it,' she whispered. 'Not holy prayers. Human ones. Please let this day last. Please let them arrive. Please, not yet.' Her fingers glowed with soft gold as she tried to soothe the trapped wishes, but the light arrived late, blooming three heartbeats after her mana moved.",
                "Helena took the hourglass gently. For a moment the frost inside stopped climbing. In the glass, she saw not her reflection, but a younger-looking woman with her face standing in a colorless street. The image smiled sadly before breaking apart. Helena closed her hand around the artifact and said only, 'We are going to that city.'"
              ],
