              "status": "full",
              "source": "Chapter lengkap",
              "content": [
                "Eirvalen appeared at sunset, though the sun had been behind them all day. The city sat in a basin of blue-white snow, encircled by frozen canals and high walls shaped like interlocking clock gears. Its towers leaned inward as if listening to the great clock tower at the center. That tower rose above everything, black against the aurora, immense and silent, with a circular face larger than any cathedral window. It had no hands.",
                "Smoke rose from chimneys. Lanterns burned. People moved in the streets. It should have been comforting. Instead, the city felt like a body breathing too slowly. Every sound arrived softened: hoofbeats, market voices, a door closing, someone singing. The noises were alive, but delayed, as if the world had placed a blanket over grief and asked it to sleep.",
                "Elara touched her charm. 'There are so many souls.' Valerius swallowed. 'How many?' 'All of them,' she said. 'Too many times.' Kael checked the gatehouse and found no guards, only two suits of armor standing empty on either side of the entrance. Their shadows held spears.",
                "Helena stood before the gate and looked up at the handless clock. For a moment, in the dark glass of its face, she saw the woman with her face from Iron-Peak's lower heart. The reflection placed one finger to her lips. Not yet. Then the gate opened by itself."
              ],
              "subArc": "Sub-Arc A: The Snow Between Seconds",
              "summary": "Eirvalen appeared at sunset, though the sun had been behind them all day. The city sat in a basin of blue-white snow, encircled by frozen canals and high walls shaped like interlocking clock gears. Its..."
