              "status": "full",
              "source": "Chapter lengkap",
              "content": [
                "The door opened into last year. Not Helena's last year, nor Eirvalen's, but a generic last year the tower seemed to keep for visitors. Dust lay thicker than it had outside. A calendar on the wall displayed thirteen months, several of which Valerius insisted did not exist. A vase held fresh flowers that had died long ago and were waiting for permission to wilt.",
                "Inside, staircases moved only when unobserved. Corridors rearranged based on memory. Maerin guided them with the clock hand that always pointed toward Helena, though he apologized whenever it suggested rude shortcuts through walls.",
                "They found rooms of civic records, all meticulously kept. Births. Marriages. Construction permits. Emergency bell schedules. The ordinary bureaucracy of a city preparing to live forever by accident. Helena lingered over a page listing bread subsidies for low-income households. Great tragedies often survived in songs. Good governments survived in paperwork no one praised.",
                "Near the archive's end, a black door waited with no handle. On it was engraved a sentence: The Regent saved the city from correction. Beneath it, scratched by a different hand, were the words: Did he?"
              ],
              "subArc": "Sub-Arc C: The Clock Tower Without a Shadow",
              "summary": "The door opened into last year. Not Helena's last year, nor Eirvalen's, but a generic last year the tower seemed to keep for visitors. Dust lay thicker than it had outside. A calendar on the..."
