                "The Zenith Rose turns south after Eirvalen, crossing a sky washed clean by thawing time. Helena watches the hourless watch from Regent Caelrith rest in her palm while the hands it does not have still seem to point toward Eleanor.",
                "Kael expects an ambush from monsters; Valerius expects a scholarly disaster; Elara expects the Holy See to object to everything. Helena expects, with a discomfort she cannot name, that the kingdom which worships her may know less about her than a dead city did.",
                "The watch gives one cold pulse whenever the Golden Tree crest appears on a distant road marker.",
                "Valerius wrote notes until the wind threatened to steal them; Elara spoke gently with travelers who asked whether the Saintess had truly met the Ancient Sage; Kael watched every roadside shrine as if one might draw a knife. Helena let them do these things. She was learning that returning to Eleanor did not mean returning home. It meant walking into a house that had kept her portrait while forgetting the sound of her voice.",
                "Eleanor waits below them, bright as a memory polished too often."
