                "They descend near the eastern provinces of Eleanor, where roads are paved with pale stone and statues of the Ancient Sage stand at every crossroads. Each statue is wrong in a different way: too tall, too holy, too beautiful, too certain.",
                "Helena laughs at first, but the laughter thins when she notices that some statues carry the sapphire cross in their eyes while others show a six-pointed star. No modern sculptor should know that shape.",
                "A provincial schoolmaster recites a children's rhyme claiming the Ancient Sage was born from moonlight under the Golden Tree.",
                "By sunset, Helena understood why the capital frightened her more than Frost-Bight's monsters. Monsters announced their hunger honestly. Eleanor's devotion wore perfume, music, children's songs, temple bells, and marble. If something had hidden inside that devotion, it had chosen the safest possible armor: love offered by people who did not know the whole truth.",
                "Helena touches one marble hand and feels the stone flinch as if corrected by an invisible scribe."
