                "At night, a hidden staircase appears beneath her room, leading to a cellar where the old foundation stones predate the capital. On one stone, a child's handwriting has been preserved by accident.",
                "It reads: Helena promised she would come back before the moon forgot us.",
                "The journey carried more than distance. Each road sign, shrine, and polished statue forced Helena to compare the living world against the version of herself people had built for comfort. She did not hate them for it. That was the difficult part. The lies had fed children, steadied soldiers, and helped frightened villages survive winter. A false legend could still shelter real hearts, and that made correcting it feel less like victory and more like surgery.",
