                "The first shelf Helena touches rearranges itself from Founding Myths to Witness Accounts to Apologies Not Delivered.",
                "Every discovery in the archive made the air thinner. Not physically; the wards maintained perfect ventilation. But with each contradiction, each erased line, each preserved apology, Helena felt the comfortable shape of her past loosen. It did not collapse. That might have been easier. Instead, it shifted by a finger's width, enough to make every old memory stand at a slightly wrong angle.",
                "A single book falls open to an empty page that smells like winter and iron."
