                "Court politics tested a different kind of patience. Helena could stop a spell faster than a thought, but she could not stop a minister from using twelve sentences to say no. The palace taught her that power wore many forms: a sword, a seal, a budget, a genealogy, a rumor placed carefully at dinner. Some were more exhausting than dragons.",
                "The memory smiles and gives her a key made of amber."
