                "Kael dislikes every word in that sentence. Helena dislikes that she understands it emotionally before she understands it intellectually.",
                "The archive floor reveals a map of the swamp as it once was, including a sealed chamber marked Not for Helena.",
                "The records here did not accuse anyone directly. That made them worse. They offered preserved cups, copied children's handwriting, ruined maps, half-burned prayers, and dates that refused to be counted. Helena had endured battlefields with less emotional cruelty. A sword could only cut where it landed. Evidence could cut backward through memory.",
                "Naturally, Helena goes there."
