                "The final shelf did not feel dramatic. That unsettled Helena more than thunder would have. Great truths, she was learning, rarely arrived with proper manners. They slipped into hands as small books, unfinished letters, watches without hands, and titles that made the heart recognize danger before the mind could translate it.",
