                "Helena asks whether he knew about the book. Astraeon answers with silence first, then with the truth she dislikes most: Yes.",
                "By the time moonlight began flowing west, the arc of the next journey had already chosen its shape. Not a command, Helena reminded herself. A shape. Commands could be refused. Shapes could be understood, altered, and, when necessary, walked through with a wooden staff and an unreasonable amount of kindness.",
